#### Event plane resolution

Finally we have a resolution correction factor which is found as described in sec. 3.2. The relative magnitude of the corrections is the correlator of the east and west planes: \(\cos\left(\Psi_{1,W}-\Psi_{1,E}\right)\), the actual values are found by inverting Bessel equations (eq. 3.7) using the sub event plane resolution. This resolution is solved for each central value of the sub-event plane resolution as well as the statistical error bars. Of course the statistical error bars of the sub-event plane resolution are symmetric, but this is not guaranteed when they are put through the root finding algorithm. If the sizes of the up and down error bars differed by less than a percent I just defined the error bar to be the average of them. In fact the difference was less than 1% every time so I never had to consider what to do in case of asymmetry. The values are

